## Science & engineering narrative (for “About” / long-form alignment)

Summarized from [`/pages/about`](https://airtulip.co/pages/about)—use for **marketing tone**, not clinical claims unless substantiated:

1. **Laminar airflow:** Single-direction, ultra-low-turbulence stream forming a stable barrier vs chaotic room/HVAC mixing; analogous to cleanrooms / controlled environments.
2. **Origin story:** Pandemic-era NYC; lasers/fog visualization; cleanroom + aerospace mental model; “filter + **control** how air moves.”
3. **Founder:** **Arjen de Jong** — aerospace engineer/physicist, **PhD in aeroacoustics**; Porsche/Ferrari/NASA-relevant experience (as stated on site); family background in cleanrooms/industrial air.
4. **External validation / partners named on site:** LaVision (laser imaging); **TU Delft** / Prof. Fulvio Scarano (flow visualization); **TU Eindhoven** Building Physics chambers (thermal mannequin, smoke); CFturbo / aerospace fan design; **owl biomimicry** (serrated blade edges for noise/turbulence).
5. **Manufacturing story:** **Brooklyn & Detroit**; hand assembly, limited batches, modular/long-life positioning; **3D-printed** aerodynamic components.
6. **IP:** “Patent-pending” / **multiple patent applications** (site language).
7. **Credibility moments:** **Kickstarter** launch; **Shark Tank**; early advocate **NFL Matt Judon** (site copy).

**Four pillars (site structure):** Aerodynamics (Delft-inspired CFD/pressure); Measurement (LaVision, sensors); Simulation & Design (CFturbo, 3D-printed paths); Real-world testing (TU/e chambers, smoke/mannequin).

