## Health & air-quality messaging (careful copy rules)

The site discusses **PM10 / PM2.5 / ultrafine** particles, sleep-related exposure, and links to **NIH / WHO / AHA / PubMed**-style references on the About page—for **educational framing**.

**For theme/section copy:**

- Prefer **experience** language: sleep quality, congestion, triggers, recovery, “clean zone,” “breathing zone.”
- Avoid **disease treatment** claims unless legal/clinical approves; mirror PDP FAQ tone (“can alleviate,” “many customers report,” etc.).
- **Consistency:** Site mixes stats (e.g. **99.997%** vs **99.97%** vs **99.995%** at 0.3 µm)—**pick one approved string** from PDP/legal before reusing in new sections.
- Strong quantitative claims (“**1,000× cleaner** than traditional purifiers,” “within **seconds**,” “**2,600 gallons** per night”) appear on marketing surfaces—treat as **approved marketing claims** only if compliance has signed off; otherwise soften or quote PDP verbatim.

